            <h2><i class="fas fa-gavel"></i> Other Rules</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Players choose their projected winners of each matchup in a round. You can submit picks for any games that haven't tipped off yet &mdash; even if other games in the same round have already started.</li>
                <li><strong>Honesty Clause:</strong> Do not look at any player's picks for the round until you submit your own!</li>
                <li>Bonus Scoring: Before the start of the tournament, players will also choose a Final Four team from each region, and a Champion:</li>
                <ul>
                    <li>5 bonus points are awarded for each initial Final Four pick to successfully reach the Final Four</li>
                    <li>10 bonus points are awarded for picking the correct Champion before the tournament begins</li>
                </ul>
            </ul>

            <h2><i class="fas fa-clock"></i> Per-Game Tipoff & Late Picks</h2>
            <p>Each game has its own tipoff time. You can submit picks as long as at least one game in the round hasn't started yet. Here's how it works:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Games that haven't started:</strong> Your pick is accepted normally.</li>
                <li><strong>Games that have already started (no draft saved):</strong> Your pick is marked as "late" and will be scored as a loss for that game, regardless of the outcome.</li>
                <li><strong>Games that have already started (with a saved draft):</strong> Your saved draft pick is used automatically and is <em>not</em> penalized. This is the safety net for when you forget to submit on time.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>If <em>all</em> games in a round have already started, you cannot submit picks at all.</p>

            <h2><i class="fas fa-save"></i> Draft Picks &amp; Early Picking</h2>

            <p>Once the Round 1 matchups are set (usually Selection Sunday), you can start filling in your picks immediately &mdash; you don't have to wait until game day.</p>

            <h3>How it works:</h3>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Pick early.</strong> Open the picks page any time after matchups are announced. Fill in your picks and click <em>"Save Draft"</em> to store them. Your selections are saved but not final.</li>
                <li><strong>Come back and submit.</strong> Before the first games tip off, return to the picks page, review your draft, and click <em>"Submit"</em> to lock them in officially.</li>
                <li><strong>Forgot to submit?</strong> No problem. When a game's tipoff time arrives, any draft pick you had saved for that game is <strong>automatically locked in for you</strong> &mdash; as if you had submitted it on time. No late penalty.</li>
            </ol>

            <div class="well well-sm" style="margin-top: 12px; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92); color: #1f2933; border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);">
                <strong><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i> The first weekend is tight.</strong> Round 2 can start as early as Saturday noon &mdash; just a day after some Round 1 games finish on Friday. Save your Round 2 draft picks as soon as you see your matchups. If Saturday sneaks up on you, your drafts have your back.
            </div>

            <h3>The fine print:</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Drafts <strong>auto-save every 60 seconds</strong> while you're on the picks page. You can also save manually at any time.</li>
                <li>Drafts are <em>not</em> final. Saving a draft does not count as submitting. Only clicking "Submit" makes your picks official &mdash; unless tipoff beats you to it (see above).</li>
                <li>If a game tips off and you have <em>no</em> draft pick saved for that game, any pick you submit afterward counts as late and will be scored as a loss, regardless of the outcome.</li>
                <li>You can submit picks for the games that haven't started yet even while other games in the round are already in progress.</li>
            </ul>
            
